{"archetypes":[{"name":"contract-drift","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan introduces optional trailer grammar that must be stated identically across six doc/script surfaces; inconsistent prose around blank-line stop, last-match-wins, and anchored regex would silently permit non-conforming implementations.","prompt_body":"Read `skills/design/scripts/check-plan-size.sh` and `skills/design/scripts/check-plan-size.md` to extract the canonical definition of the new optional trailer grammar: exact anchored regex forms, blank-line scan-stop semantics, last-match-wins rule within the final contiguous metadata block, and the four new output keys. Then read `skills/design/SKILL.md`, `skills/design/references/flags.md`, `skills/design/references/approval-gates.md`, and `skills/design/references/discussion-rounds.md` to verify each surface's prose agrees precisely with the canonical definition. Flag any surface where the blank-line stop rule, the last-match-wins semantics, or the exact regex constraint is omitted, paraphrased ambiguously, or contradicted. Also check that the `SOFT_ADVISORY` key name and the `TRIGGER_REASONS` priority order (`plan-body-lines` before `diff-added`/`diff-lines`) are stated consistently across all doc surfaces. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"revision-preservation","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan enforces trailer preservation mechanically in the waterfall script but only through prompt-side snapshot/validate language for Gate A and Gate B direct rewrites — an asymmetry that could leave prompt-driven revision paths undetectable by any automated harness.","prompt_body":"The plan specifies script-enforced preservation for waterfall candidates (post-apply validation in `skills/design/scripts/revise-plan-with-waterfall.sh`) but prompt-side-only snapshot-and-validate contracts for Gate A discussion rewrites and Gate B direct rewrites in `skills/design/references/discussion-rounds.md` and `skills/design/references/approval-gates.md`. For each of these four revision entry points, check whether the assigned test coverage is commensurate: note that `scripts/test-design-structure.sh` contains-checks on prose are the only harness for the Gate A and Gate B paths. Assess whether a Gate A or Gate B rewrite could silently drop optional trailers without any automated regression catching it, and whether the plan adequately addresses this gap or proposes a structural enforcement mechanism. Also verify the plan specifies what `revise-plan-with-waterfall.sh` should do when the original plan contains no optional trailers — does the post-apply validation still run, and is the no-trailers case treated as pass or skip. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"harness-completeness","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan lists nine failure modes and multiple edge cases but does not always specify concrete fixture details — gaps between a named failure mode and a fully determined test case would leave regressions undetectable.","prompt_body":"Read `skills/design/scripts/test-check-plan-size.sh` and `skills/design/scripts/test-check-plan-size.md` to understand the existing assert patterns and case numbering. Cross-reference the plan's nine failure modes and edge-case list against the new test cases proposed in the plan, and for each failure mode verify that at least one named test case provides a fully determined fixture and assertion that would catch a regression. Pay particular attention to: failure mode 5 (spoof resistance — does the plan specify a concrete fixture embedding `mechanical_churn: true` inside a prose paragraph or fenced code block, and does it assert which metadata block wins?); failure mode 8 (metadata false positive — does the 800-body-plus-trailers case explicitly assert `PLAN_LINES=800`?); and failure mode 9 (unified-diff bypass — does the `test-plan-review-loop.sh` extension actually invoke a revision path through the waterfall or only assert on the final `LOOP_STATUS` variable?). Flag any failure mode with no corresponding test case or with an underdetermined fixture that cannot unambiguously verify the intended invariant. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
